# Build and test (iOS)

**Canonical procedure:** `AGENTS.md > Build and test`, the single source of truth for all agent tools. Follow it exactly; don't duplicate it here.

## Quick reference

After any substantive Swift, SwiftUI, or Xcode change, run from the repo root:

1. `make gate` (`bash scripts/gate.sh`) — tool versions, format and lint on changed Swift files, script tests, bare compile. No simulator. Logs to `tmp/gate.log`, stops at the first failure.
2. `make focused-tests ONLY=<target>/<Class>[/<test>]` — only the tests you added or changed, on one simulator.

The full unit and UI suites run in PR CI; run `make unit-tests` / `make ui-tests` locally only when you need to. To wait on a CI run, use `bash scripts/wait_ci.sh <run-id> [pr#]` — never a hand-written `until … sleep … done` loop.

Simulator pinning (`SIMULATOR_UDID`, `SIMULATOR_NAME`), deployment-target rules, scheme name, and rationale: see `AGENTS.md > Build and test`.
